From 678aec4bc7a3c7f6d72ce96eddd1b277747e7bb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew <matthewhale@live.com.au>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 21:50:29 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 32/59] XvT self-balancing shields and throttle-dependent
 turning

- game.xvt_shields: when the player's shields take damage (lasers, warheads,
  collisions), the hit bank takes half the difference from the other bank
  and the distribution returns to even, as XvT does. Diverting to front or
  rear still works until the next hit on the weaker side.
- game.xvt_turning: player pitch/yaw/roll gain follows XvT's throttle curve,
  full at 1/3 throttle, 2/3 at full throttle, 1/3 when stopped, plus XvT's
  ~5% per step laser+shield recharge term.
- Game page: "Shield Hits" and "Turning" selectors.
